  "rule": "(2*active_weight if weight >= neighbor_cover else 0) + weight + residual_pack - 0.2*max(0,residual_cover-residual_pack) - 0.3*max(0,neighbor_pack-weight) + 0.02*weight*boundary_edges/max(1,degree*max(0,remaining_count-1-degree))",
  "rationale": "Both parents are identical: their backbone combines root reward, pack/cover estimates of the compatible remainder, neighborhood opportunity cost, and conflict structure. Explore certified exchange before ordinary continuation ranking. When root weight reaches the active neighborhood's clique-cover upper bound, replacing any selected neighbors by the root cannot decrease reward, so give that choice a separate priority tier. Otherwise emphasize feasible residual packing, discount uncertainty through the cover-minus-pack gap, and penalize stronger neighborhood alternatives. A small boundary-density bonus favors removing conflicts that constrain the surviving remainder."
